	from sfmc68@verizon.net on Sun, Feb 26, 2006 at 10:26:00AM -0500
References: <4401C888.8040906@verizon.net>
Message-ID: <20060226103447.A11596@linux04.mro.cpqcorp.net>

On Sun, Feb 26, 2006 at 10:26:00AM -0500, bob wrote:
>
> I just installed AC2 on a DS10, ATI 7500, Dell P1110 mon.
> Install is fine, BUT It did not recognize my monitor, and did not give 
> me a chance to select the monotor. Probably something I did.
> 
> Can someone point me to the docs on how to change the monitor setting?
> or tell me what I might have missed on the install?

In the Section "Monitor" area, add:

	HorizSync ww-xx
	VertRefresh yy-zz

where ww-xx is the horizontal sync range of that Dell monitor,
and yy-zz is its vertical refresh range.

For example, for a COMPAQ P110 monitor one might use:

	HorizSync 31.5-95
	VertRefresh 50-160

Oh, you may need to edit the Section "Display" area as well, adding
appropriate "Modes" lines to the various depth-related SubSections.
Example:

        Subsection "Display"
                Depth       16
                Modes       "1280x1024" "1024x768" "800x600" "640x480"
        EndSubsection

Good luck.

 --Jay++

